<div class="snp">
  <div class="snp__head">
    <p class="snp__eyebrow">Terms and policies</p>
    <h2 class="snp__title">Privacy policy</h2>
    <p class="snp__lead">What information we keep about you, why we keep it – and how you stay in control of it.</p>
    <p class="snp__date">Last updated October 7, 2026</p>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__facts">
    <div class="snp__fact"><span class="snp__fact-val">Never</span><span class="snp__fact-lbl">do we sell your information</span></div>
    <div class="snp__fact"><span class="snp__fact-val">Your choice</span><span class="snp__fact-lbl">on statistics and marketing cookies</span></div>
    <div class="snp__fact"><span class="snp__fact-val">30 days</span><span class="snp__fact-lbl">to answer your request</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__toc">
    <p class="snp__toc-title">Contents</p>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#controller">Who is responsible</a></li>
      <li><a href="#collect">Information we collect</a></li>
      <li><a href="#purposes">Purposes and how long we keep it</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sharing">Who we share it with</a></li>
      <li><a href="#transfers">Where your information is processed</a></li>
      <li><a href="#cookies">Cookies</a></li>
      <li><a href="#newsletter">Newsletter and emails</a></li>
      <li><a href="#security">How we protect your information</a></li>
      <li><a href="#rights">Your rights</a></li>
      <li><a href="#changes">Changes</a></li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__sec" id="controller">
    <h3><span class="snp__num">01</span>Who is responsible</h3>
    <div class="snp__body">
      <p>The Dalton Pierce store is run by Stilhuset Nord, Luboszewy 46, 97-217 Luboszewy, Poland, NIP 7732509014, REGON 528999874, which is responsible for the personal information collected through this store. You can reach us at <a href="mailto:support@daltonpierce.com">support@daltonpierce.com</a>.</p>
      <p>We are a company based in the European Union, so we handle your information under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). For customers in Canada, we also follow the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act (PIPEDA) and any provincial privacy law that applies.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__sec" id="collect">
    <h3><span class="snp__num">02</span>Information we collect</h3>
    <div class="snp__body">
      <p><strong>Information you give us</strong> – when you place an order, create an account, sign up for the newsletter or write to customer service:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Name, delivery address, email and phone number</li>
        <li>Order details: items, sizes, prices and payment method (not your card number)</li>
        <li>The content of your messages to us, e.g. photos for a defect claim</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Information collected automatically</strong> when you use the site:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address, browser, device type and operating system</li>
        <li>Which pages you visit, when and for how long, and what you add to your cart</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We only collect statistics and marketing data if you have agreed to those cookies.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__sec" id="purposes">
    <h3><span class="snp__num">03</span>Purposes and how long we keep it</h3>
    <div class="snp__body">
      <div class="snp__table">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Information</th><th>Legal basis</th><th>How long</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Processing and delivering your order</td><td>Name, address, email, phone, order details</td><td>Performing our contract with you (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b))</td><td>As long as needed for the order and any defect claim (2 years)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Accounting</td><td>Order and payment details</td><td>Legal obligation (Art. 6(1)(c)), accounting law</td><td>5 years from the end of the financial year</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Customer service</td><td>Your message and order number</td><td>Performing the contract and legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(b) and (f))</td><td>Up to 2 years after the matter is closed</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Customer account</td><td>Name, email, addresses, order history</td><td>Performing the contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td><td>Until you delete the account</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Newsletter</td><td>Email</td><td>Your consent (Art. 6(1)(a))</td><td>Until you unsubscribe</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Cart reminders</td><td>Email and cart contents</td><td>Legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f)) – you can always opt out</td><td>Up to 30 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Statistics and marketing</td><td>Device and usage data via cookies</td><td>Your consent (Art. 6(1)(a))</td><td>See the cookie banner</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Fraud prevention</td><td>Order, payment and device data</td><td>Legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f))</td><td>As long as necessary</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>We never store your card details – they're handled by the payment provider. We don't make decisions about you based solely on automated processing.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__sec" id="sharing">
    <h3><span class="snp__num">04</span>Who we share it with</h3>
    <div class="snp__body">
      <p>We never sell, rent or trade your information. We share it only with those who help us run the store – and only what they need:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Shopify</strong> – the platform the store and checkout run on</li>
        <li><strong>Payment providers</strong> – to complete and secure your payment</li>
        <li><strong>Carriers</strong> – name, address, email and phone for delivery and tracking</li>
        <li><strong>Our makers</strong> – name, address and phone when an item ships directly from their warehouse</li>
        <li><strong>Klaviyo</strong> – sending the newsletter, order emails and reminders</li>
        <li><strong>Meta (Facebook and Instagram)</strong> – measuring ads, only if you have consented</li>
        <li><strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> – statistics on how the site is used, only if you have consented</li>
        <li>Authorities where the law requires it, and advisers such as accountants and lawyers</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If the store is sold or merged with another company, your information may pass to the new owner, who must handle it under the same rules.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__sec" id="transfers">
    <h3><span class="snp__num">05</span>Where your information is processed</h3>
    <div class="snp__body">
      <p>We process your information ourselves in the European Union. Some of our service providers process data outside Canada and the EU, including in the United States and – when an item ships directly from a maker's warehouse – in the country where that warehouse is located. These transfers rely on safeguards such as the European Commission's standard contractual clauses or the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, so your information stays protected. While it is held abroad, it may be accessible to the courts and authorities of that country under local law.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__sec" id="cookies">
    <h3><span class="snp__num">06</span>Cookies</h3>
    <div class="snp__body">
      <p>Cookies are small files stored in your browser. We use three kinds:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Necessary</strong> – make the cart, checkout and security work. They don't require consent.</li>
        <li><strong>Statistics</strong> – show us how the site is used so we can improve it. Only with your consent.</li>
        <li><strong>Marketing</strong> – measure whether our ads work and show relevant ads. Only with your consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You make your choice in the cookie banner the first time you visit. You can change it at any time via the <em>Cookie settings</em> link at the bottom of the page, or delete cookies in your browser.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__sec" id="newsletter">
    <h3><span class="snp__num">07</span>Newsletter and emails</h3>
    <div class="snp__body">
      <p>You only receive the newsletter if you've signed up yourself. You can unsubscribe with one click at the bottom of every email. We always send order confirmations and shipping emails, because they're part of your purchase.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__sec" id="security">
    <h3><span class="snp__num">08</span>How we protect your information</h3>
    <div class="snp__body">
      <ul>
        <li>All traffic on the site runs over an encrypted connection (SSL).</li>
        <li>Only people who need it for their work have access to your information.</li>
        <li>We use service providers that protect personal information to the required standard, under data processing agreements.</li>
        <li>If a security breach could harm you, we'll notify you and the relevant authorities as the law requires.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The site isn't directed at children under 16, and we don't knowingly collect information about them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__sec" id="rights">
    <h3><span class="snp__num">09</span>Your rights</h3>
    <div class="snp__body">
      <p>You have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access the information we hold about you</li>
        <li>have incorrect information corrected</li>
        <li>have your information deleted when we no longer need it – although we must keep accounting records for 5 years</li>
        <li>restrict or object to how we use it</li>
        <li>receive your information in a common format (data portability)</li>
        <li>withdraw your consent at any time</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Write to <a href="mailto:support@daltonpierce.com">support@daltonpierce.com</a> – we reply within 30 days. If you're unhappy with how we handle your information, you can complain to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada, <a href="https://www.priv.gc.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.priv.gc.ca</a>, or to our supervisory authority in Poland, Urząd Ochrony Danych Osobowych, <a href="https://uodo.gov.pl" target="_blank" rel="noopener">uodo.gov.pl</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__sec" id="changes">
    <h3><span class="snp__num">10</span>Changes</h3>
    <div class="snp__body">
      <p>We update this policy when we change the way we handle information. The date at the top shows the latest change. If the change is significant, we'll let you know on the site or by email.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__help">
    <p class="snp__help-title">Questions about your information?</p>
    <p>Write to us and we'll help you with access, correction or deletion.</p>
    <a class="snp__btn" href="mailto:support@daltonpierce.com?subject=Personal%20information">Write to us</a>
    <p class="snp__help-meta">support@daltonpierce.com · Mon–Fri 9:00–18:00 CET</p>
  </div>

  <div class="snp__more">
